                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I think I've played enough to give my opinion on this game.  I like it.  I don't want to stop playing, I got that \"just one more turn!\" bug.\n\nQuick note before I go further, this is a PC port of a phone game, so if you are biased against phone games you might want to keep that in mind.  However, I think there's a free version out there you could try to see if you like the gameplay.  And if you want to complain about having to pay for something that is free in a different format, I'd like to remind you that on Steam this game has trading cards which you can sell to make back some of your money.  And the price isn't bad, $5 seems right.  If you have issues about price, then wait for a sale.\n\nThis game is a tactical turn-based card game.  You have a deck of cards with fighter charcters (and animals), weapons and armor, and other items that affect buffs and debuffs.  There is a main story but there's also online PVP.  So far I've only been playing the story against the AI.\n\nIn this game you lose if your commander gets killed, so guard him (or her) carefully.  It's like the king in chess.  Checkmate and it's game over.  You can choose who the commander is when you start each level.  \n\nCharacters have various levels of attack strength, movement range, etc.  Some can only attack in four directions (up, down, left, righ) while others can attack diagonally also.  Some have to be right next to the enemy to attack, others can be one space away to attack with a bow.  You can equip armor and weapons if you get those cards drawn.  At the start of the game you get 5 cards and one card each turn.  It's random so you never know what you're going to get.  Part of the difficulty is that some of the characters are better with specific weapons (the archer gets a bonus for using a bow) but if you didn't get the right cards you might have to give your archer a sword or else wait and hope you get the bow card.  \n\nThere are also animals that fight for you.  You start with pigs (sow).  They can't equip anything, except if you get the collar card later on.  I just got another animal or creature but haven't gotten to use it yet.\n\nAs you can see from the screenshots the gameplay takes place on a grid.  The colors represent where your characters can move.  There are barriers that you have to move around, though remember some characters can attack diagonally and what seems to be a solid line of mountains actually might have a gap.\n\nYou get money (gold) after each level.  Use that to buy card packs to get more cards.  There is also crafting to level up your cards.  I haven't experimented much with that yet because I haven't gotten many extra cards yet.\n\nGraphics look kind of old school.  If you don't like that sort of look, then you can decide from the screenshots.  I personally don't care what a game looks like if the gameplay is good.\n\nI can't think of anything else to say right now.  I might update this review later on as I play more of the game.",
